# Release signing credentials. Copy to `android/key.properties` and fill in -
# or keep the passwords out of every file and set ABSENSAS_SIGNING_* instead.
#
# This file is an example and is committed. `key.properties` itself is not, and
# must never be: it names a keystore and carries its passwords.
# Keystore files (*.jks, *.keystore, *.p12, *.pfx) must NEVER be placed in this
# repository.
#
# A debug build needs none of this. Gradle only asks for these when a release is
# actually being built (`assembleRelease` / `bundleRelease`), and refuses to
# produce an unsigned one — see `android/app/build.gradle.kts`.
#
# Retired keys: a release whose keystore file is named `upload-keystore.jks` or
# `esas-keystore.jks` is refused for com.absensas.app. Sign with the Absensas key.
#
# Every value below can come from the environment instead, and the environment
# wins over this file: ABSENSAS_SIGNING_STORE_FILE, ABSENSAS_SIGNING_STORE_PASSWORD,
# ABSENSAS_SIGNING_KEY_ALIAS, ABSENSAS_SIGNING_KEY_PASSWORD,
# ABSENSAS_SIGNING_STORE_TYPE. For example, passwords from the macOS Keychain:
#
#   # once each; `-w` last makes `security` prompt for the value
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s absensas-signing-store -w
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s absensas-signing-key -w
#
#   # per build; nothing is written to disk or to shell history
#   ABSENSAS_SIGNING_STORE_PASSWORD="$(security find-generic-password -s absensas-signing-store -w)" \
#   ABSENSAS_SIGNING_KEY_PASSWORD="$(security find-generic-password -s absensas-signing-key -w)" \
#   flutter build apk --release

# Path to the keystore OUTSIDE the repository. A leading `~/` is expanded.
storeFile=~/.absensas-signing/absensas-app-signing.p12
storePassword=
keyAlias=absensas
keyPassword=
# Optional: PKCS12 is assumed for .p12/.pfx; otherwise the JDK default, which
# reads PKCS12 and JKS keystores alike.
# storeType=PKCS12
